## 7. Legacy: `backend_old/` and pre-`members-core` frontend

Only relevant if you're working on features still tied to the old system (anything the sidebar shows greyed out):

```bash
cd backend_old
source .venv/bin/activate   # or: python3 -m venv .venv && pip install -r requirements.txt
uvicorn app:app --reload --port 8000
```
It uses its own `chrch_collections` Postgres database, its own `.env`, and its own auth/token system — entirely separate from `api/`. `migrate.py` (Access `.accdb` → SQL) and `init_members.py` (seed `members` from `Members.xlsx`) also belong to this legacy backend.

